# rule.forbid.itemization-without-coordinates

whenever you itemize an enumerable concept, name the artifact by its coordinates: every segment a `$key=$value` pair. a bare word is a violation.

```
$kind.of=$concept._.md                      # SUMMARY — axes, counts, gaps
$kind.of=$concept.$dimension=$position.md   # one ENTRY per member — always
```

the kind (inventory, catalog, ejected example) does not change the name; both files are owed.

```
inventory.of=fulcrums._.md              catalog.of=archetype._.md
inventory.of=fulcrums.case=F14-slug.md  catalog.of=archetype.kind=article.md
```

`example=$id` is the same form (`term=$x._.choice.example=$id`).

## .the case dimension

for occurrences (fulcrum, incident, review round) the dimension is `case`. an ordinal is not an id:

```
👎  case=F14
👍  case=F14-entoolment-ladder-is-fluid-rigid-solid
```

join with a hyphen, never a dot (a dot is the segment separator).

## .the test

am i about to itemize an enumerable concept? yes → name is coordinates, both files owed. settle the name before the kind: the kind question feels like the name question and is not.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you name an entry after what it is about | name it after where it sits |
| a filename holds a value with no `$dimension=` | make the axis explicit |
| you write the summary only, or entries only | the other is owed too |
| you use `1.`, `2.` to order entries | order belongs in the summary |
| entries list dimensions in different order | fix one order |
| a cell cannot exist | it still gets its file (the invariant) |

blocker: entry not entirely `$dimension=$position` segments · bare position · summary with no entries · entries with no summary · inconsistent dimension order · ordinal prefixes · bare-ordinal `case=` · forbidden cell with no file · itemization under a prose name (`catalog.md`, `register.md`) · ejected member named by aught but a coordinate.

⇒ `rule.require.summary-at-the-cluster-root` · `rule.require.inventory-for-enumerable-concepts`
